course: dictionary
lesson: 16093
title: Waterfowl: birds of the water
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word's context is the words around it, and they often give clues to its meaning. «The lake was full of waterfowl, with ducks and geese paddling side by side.» Lakes, paddling, ducks and geese all point to birds that live on water, so waterfowl must mean water birds.
explain: Look inside the word for more clues. Water is in it, and so is a bird. Waterfowl are birds that swim and live on or near water, especially ducks, geese and swans. «A swan glided past the waterfowl at the lake's edge» shows swans and other waterfowl together. Always check: does your meaning fit the sentence?
explain: The word is the same for one bird or many. «One waterfowl sat on the pond.» and «Ten waterfowl sat on the pond.» both use waterfowl. A park may have a waterfowl reserve, a place where wild water birds are protected.
fact: Waterfowl are birds that swim and live on or near water.
fact: Ducks, geese and swans are all waterfowl.
fact: Waterfowl is the same word for one bird or many birds.
fact: Many waterfowl have webbed feet, waterproof feathers and flat beaks to help them live on water.
fact: Many waterfowl migrate, which means they travel long distances with the seasons.
exercise: «The pond was full of waterfowl, paddling and diving.» What are waterfowl? | Plants that grow in ponds | Stones that sink to the bottom | *Birds that swim and live on or near water | Fish that swim in the deep sea
exercise: Ducks, geese and swans are all examples of what? | Insects | Reptiles | *Waterfowl | Mammals
exercise: Which feature helps waterfowl swim? | Thick fur to keep warm | *Webbed feet | Sharp teeth for hunting | Long claws for climbing trees
test: In «One waterfowl rested on the lake» and «Ten waterfowl rested on the lake», how does the word change? | *It does not change | It becomes waterfowled | It adds an -s to become waterfowls | It changes into a different word
test: «The waterfowl reserve in the park keeps wild water birds safe.» What is a waterfowl reserve? | *A place set aside to protect water birds | A school for swimming lessons | A shop that sells fishing rods | A park with a big playground
exam: Which word best describes ducks, geese and swans? | Reptiles | Mammals | Fish | *Waterfowl
